# Normalize line endings to LF in the repo *and* the working tree.
#
# Why: the Sandcastle sandbox runs on Linux (LF) while this host is Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true → CRLF). Without this file, every file an agent touches
# is recorded as a full-file rewrite (CRLF↔LF), bloating each merge with
# thousands of lines of pure line-ending noise. eol=lf makes the sandbox and
# host agree. The deploy target (Raspberry Pi) is Linux, so LF is also correct
# at runtime. .gitattributes overrides core.autocrlf per path.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch their bytes.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico  binary
*.gif  binary
